        },
        "description": "Searches the data sources by keyword and returns ranked endpoint summaries, each identified by provider, endpoint, and endpoint_version, with its price and run mode. Several providers may sell the same capability; the ranking is relevance-only and the price is shown alongside so the caller chooses. Pages are short by default (5, up to 20): read `total` for how many candidates exist, then pass next_cursor back as cursor for the next page; the cursor is bound to the query. The list is already scoped to the calling key's effective policy: every endpoint in it is one this key can run. Each hit carries a `score`, the cosine similarity between the query and that endpoint's description: use it to compare rows, and inspect an endpoint before running it. The ranking returns its nearest candidates rather than withholding them, so neither a page of low scores nor reaching the last page shows that a capability is absent — try other words before concluding that.",
        "summary": "Search runnable endpoints",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "query": {
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "limit": {
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "minimum": 1,
                        "maximum": 20
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "cursor": {
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "task_id": {
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "string",
                        "description": "The task this search belongs to. A search without a task_id starts a new task. The response returns its task_id. Send it on every later search, inspect and run of the same piece of work. Any stable string is accepted."
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "metadata": {
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "anyOf": [
                          {
                            "type": "object",
                            "additionalProperties": {
                              "type": "string",
                              "minLength": 1,
                              "maxLength": 500
                            },
                            "maxProperties": 20,
                            "propertyNames": {
                              "type": "string",
                              "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,39}$"
                            }
                          },
                          {}
                        ],
                        "description": "Your own key-value strings for this call, for your records: up to 20 keys (lowercase letters, digits and underscores, starting with a letter, at most 40 characters), string values of 1–500 characters. An entry that breaks these rules is dropped whole, never truncated, and the call goes ahead; the run returns the metadata that was stored. Glasser returns it on the Run and lets you filter runs by it; it never goes to a provider and never affects routing, price or idempotency. Put the id of your own end user in user_id. Use an opaque id, never an email address or a name."
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "use_case": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "description": "Required on every search. The use case behind this search: what the user asked for, in their own words, with the subject in it — the company, domain, ticker, place or topic. Shorten a long request rather than rewriting it."
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "use_case"
                ],
                "additionalProperties": false
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "x-mint": {
          "href": "/api-reference/endpoints/search"
        }
      }
    },
